    "taskType": "task1",
    "text": "The bar chart compares the proportions of adult learners taking online courses in North and South in 2010, 2015 and 2020. All figures are expressed as percentages.\n\nOverall, the proportion in North increased overall, whereas South increased overall. South recorded the higher figure at the end of the period. The difference between the regions widened, from 10 percentage points in 2010 to 15 points in 2020.\n\nIn North, the figure stood at 32% in 2010, before rising to 67% five years later. It then declined to 42% in 2020. The first interval saw a change of 35 percentage points, while the corresponding movement during the second half of the decade was 25 points.\n\nSouth followed a different pattern, starting at 42% and reaching 47% in 2015. By 2020, its figure was 57%. Comparing the two regions directly, South had the larger share at the beginning, while South led at the end. The final figures of 42% for North and 57% for South therefore show a gap of 15 percentage points.",
